cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TAS Research Suite: Topological Anomaly Score Framework for Early Warning of Critical Transitions"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the methods it implements in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Kang
    given-names: In-Su
    alias: kang-insu
    affiliation: Korea Electric Power Corporation (KEPCO)

version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2025-01-01"

abstract: >-
  TAS Research Suite implements the Topological Langevin Dynamics (TLD) framework,
  providing open-source tools for early-warning detection of critical transitions
  using Persistent Homology and Topological Data Analysis. Core components include:
  Topological Anomaly Score (TAS), Persistent Entropy (Hp), anisotropic Vietoris-Rips
  filtration, adaptive alpha-tuning via Bayesian optimisation, Topological Early Warning
  Index (TEWI), Topological Collapse Rate, and Topological Fingerprint Library.
  Applications span deep neural network learning collapse detection, power grid
  voltage instability early warning, and chaotic dynamical system transition detection.

keywords:
  - "Topological Data Analysis"
  - "Persistent Homology"
  - "Topological Anomaly Score"
  - "Persistent Entropy"
  - "Early Warning Signals"
  - "Critical Transitions"
  - "Deep Learning"
  - "Gradient Vanishing"
  - "Learning Collapse"
  - "Power Systems"
  - "Chaos Detection"
  - "Double Pendulum"
  - "Anisotropic Metric"
  - "Vietoris-Rips Filtration"
  - "Topological Langevin Dynamics"

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/kang-insu/TAS-Research-Suite"

